      "descriptionHtml": "<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abstract_art\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Abstract art\">Abstract painting</a> called <i>Artwork for living room</i> (<i>Oeuvre pour salon</i> in French) by <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Basile_Morin\" title=\"User:Basile Morin\">Basile Morin</a>, 2003. Made in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toulouse\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Toulouse\">Toulouse</a>, France. Framed <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acrylic_paint\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Acrylic paint\">acrylic</a> canva with blue rectangles. Influences: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piet_Mondrian\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Piet Mondrian\">Piet Mondrian</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Victor_Vasarely\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Victor Vasarely\">Victor Vasarely</a>. We can see this as an eye like a window: the light blue part depicts the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Visual_perception\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Visual perception\"><i>sight</i></a> and the white square the opening.\nIn 2020, by chance, strong similarities were found with the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Composition_(visual_arts)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Composition (visual arts)\">composition</a> of <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:D%C3%BClmen,_Kirchspiel,_ehem._Sondermunitionslager_Visbeck,_Bunker_--_2020_--_8365.jpg\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"File:Dülmen, Kirchspiel, ehem. Sondermunitionslager Visbeck, Bunker -- 2020 -- 8365.jpg\">this photograph</a>.",
